  "kind": "excel-differs-from-math",
  "title": "MULTINOMIAL sums log10(2..=total), subtracts log10(2..=item) in reverse argument order, and rejects total > 170",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20527, MULTINOMIAL truncates each admitted argument toward zero (negative gives #NUM!), rejects total > 170 with #NUM!, accumulates acc = sum_{k=2..=total} excel_log10(k), then loops over the flattened items in reverse order (last argument first, first argument last) subtracting excel_log10(2..=item), and finishes with POWER(10.0, acc). Because acc climbs toward log10(170!) ~ 306.8 before subtracting the item logs back down, rounding at larger exponents leaves systematic drift (up to 4,672 ULP on single-argument inputs, where acc < 0 also triggers POWER's 1.0 / p reciprocal and even LSBs) and makes MULTINOMIAL non-commutative: MULTINOMIAL(4, 108) differs from MULTINOMIAL(108, 4) by 107 ULP.",
  "status": "inferred",
  "basis": "Measured across 800 cb4 live Excel 16.0.20527 calls and prospective frozen_multinomial_cb4.jsonl (409 of 409 matched with 0 ULP max error vs 0 of 409 on prior master). Landing nx3 moved the full MULTINOMIAL witness bank from 2,569 to 2,804 of 2,804 (+235, worst ULP 4,672 -> 0).",
  "inferred": "That Excel loops in reverse item order using x87 FLDLG2/FYL2X and POWER(10, acc) is inferred from matching all 2,804 witness rows and 409 of 409 frozen holdouts.",
  "documentation": null,
